\title{Correct and Computable Specifications in Lean}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-04-20}
\taxon{Talk}

\p{\em{Abstract:} The efficacy of formal verification depends on high quality specifications which are both correct and complete. This talk will ask: What is an ideal specification? How do we evaluate and improve our specifications? And how can Lean help us achieve the highest-assurance software possible?}

